# Memory and hot path

## Allocation
- In `update` / every frame: **no** `new THREE.Vector3|Quaternion|Matrix4|Color|Array`.
- Scratch: module-level `const _pos = new THREE.Vector3()`, or `tmp` from `utils.js`, or `this._tmp` on the instance.
- `stepToward(..., stepScratch)` — caller owns the scratch; no allocation inside.

## GPU / geometry
- Terrain morph: only touched indices + `recomputeNormalsPartial` + adjacency from the `terrain` constructor.
- **Do not** call `geometry.computeVertexNormals()` on the whole planet after a morph.
- `attribute.needsUpdate = true` only when data actually changed; batch dirty flags (`_morphDirty`).
- Cap clip + `CONFIG.pixelRatioMax` / `resolutionScale` — do not tweak ad-hoc “for FPS”.

## Dispose (required on despawn)
- `geometry.dispose()`, `material.dispose()` (including arrays), textures, `light.dispose()`.
- Remove from parent group before dropping references.
- Spells: extend existing `disposeX` / `disposeObject` — do not silently leak.
- Fire: `MAX_FIRE_LIGHTS` in `burn.js` — do not add uncapped PointLights.

## Render budget (do not change without reason)
- One terrain mesh, shadow map 1024, frustum covers the whole planet (`shadowFrustumHalf`).
- No quality presets, no “low/med/high”.
- Do not change spell VFX appearance for optimization.

## Bottlenecks (watch)
- Full vertex passes / wet BFS outside the morph region.
- `clone(true)` meshes every frame (FOW ghosts only via lazy `ensure*Ghost`).
- New CanvasTexture / DataTexture in the loop — cache like `burn.js` `ensureMaps()`.
- Planet-wide instanced trees / dual terrain mesh = regression no-go.
